// The laws a country had in force on 1 January 2024, where they are not the default of their
// category (common/laws). Every country is listed the same way; a category not named here is at
// its default.
//
// Nationalities policy:
//   settlement   - China: the Han migration into Xinjiang and Tibet, boarding schools, the
//                  "bilingual" education that is Mandarin education.
//   assimilation - Russia (the 2018 law that made minority languages optional in school),
//                  Turkey (no Kurdish-medium public schooling), Iran, Myanmar, Thailand (Thai
//                  in every school, the southern Malay provinces), France (no regional
//                  language has official standing), Algeria (Arabisation).
//   pluralism    - federal or consociational states with minority-language schooling and
//                  institutions: Switzerland, Belgium, Spain, Canada, India (linguistic
//                  states), Finland, Bosnia and Herzegovina, North Macedonia (Ohrid),
//                  Ethiopia (ethnic federalism), South Africa, Bolivia, New Zealand, Iraq
//                  (Kurdistan Region), the United Kingdom (devolution).
{
  "CHN": { "laws": ["nationalities_settlement"] },
  "RUS": { "laws": ["nationalities_assimilation"] },
  "TUR": { "laws": ["nationalities_assimilation"] },
